Note on the binary-only libraries
---------------------------------

Espressif publishes its Wi-Fi, PHY and coexistence libraries under Apache-2.0 but without source code. Apache-2.0 is
compatible with the AGPL-3.0, but the AGPL asks for the "Corresponding Source" of a conveyed binary, and these libraries
have none. This is the same question every GPL-family firmware for the ESP32 has; an explicit additional permission
under AGPL section 7 for linking these libraries would settle it. No such permission is granted in this file yet.

The ESP32-S3 live view (`CAMOS_LIVE`, docs/dev/LIVE_VIEW.md) adds `esp_peer`, whose core is a binary library
licensed for use with Espressif chips only. That use restriction, and the missing source, raise the same AGPL question
in a stronger form: an image built with `CAMOS_LIVE` on should only be conveyed once the copyright holder grants an
additional permission (AGPL section 7) covering these Espressif components.
